.TH "EPX\-VENDORS" "1" "" "epx" "epx manual"
.SH "NAME"
epx\-vendors \- read and change vendors
.SH "SYNOPSIS"
.RS "4"
.nf
epx vendors [flags]
epx vendors [command]
.fi
.RE
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
Reads and changes vendors, the sellers of a marketplace tenant; \fBepx vendor\-locations\fR reads and changes their locations. create and update ID (an upsert) send the JSON body of \fB\-\-file\fR; delete ID sends none.
.PP
Its reads require the vendor.vendor_read scope. Its writes require the vendor.vendor_manage scope.
.SH "COMMANDS"
.SS "epx vendors create"
Create one vendor.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx vendors create [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Creates the vendor that the JSON body of \fB\-\-file\fR describes, shaped as \fBepx vendors get ID \-o json\fR prints one: name (required), type (COMPANY, the default, or SUBSIDIARY), parentId (the vendor a subsidiary belongs to), legalInfo, contactDetails (a list of contacts, each as \fB{"email": ...}\fR, which is all Emporix keeps of one), locations (its vendor locations, each as \fB{"id": ...}\fR or in full, as get prints it) and mixins; parentId and locations must name items that exist (400 Bad Request, exit 1, otherwise). Without an id, Emporix makes one, and answers with it; an id that exists already is a conflict (exit 5).
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends POST. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the vendor.vendor_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SS "epx vendors delete"
Delete one vendor.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx vendors delete ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Deletes the vendor ID; it sends no body. ID is the ID that \fBepx vendors list\fR shows; an unknown one is answered as one that Emporix deleted (204 No Content). Its subsidiaries stay and still name it as their parentId.
.PP
Deletes data, which cannot be undone. On a terminal, epx sends DELETE only once you type ID at its prompt. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the vendor.vendor_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal).
.SS "epx vendors get"
Show one vendor.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx vendors get ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads vendors, the sellers of a marketplace tenant. TYPE is COMPANY or SUBSIDIARY, PARENT the vendor a subsidiary belongs to and COUNTRY the country of registration. Registration details, contact details and locations are only in \fB\-o json\fR; \fBepx vendor\-locations\fR lists the locations.
.PP
Requires the vendor.vendor_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, NAME, TYPE, PARENT, LEGAL NAME, COUNTRY.
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.SS "epx vendors list"
List vendors.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx vendors list [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads vendors, the sellers of a marketplace tenant. TYPE is COMPANY or SUBSIDIARY, PARENT the vendor a subsidiary belongs to and COUNTRY the country of registration. Registration details, contact details and locations are only in \fB\-o json\fR; \fBepx vendor\-locations\fR lists the locations.
.PP
Requires the vendor.vendor_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, NAME, TYPE, PARENT, LEGAL NAME, COUNTRY.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, passed as given, e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx vendors search"
Search vendors.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx vendors search [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Reads the vendors that an Emporix q filter finds (\fB\-\-query\fR; without it, every vendor). It reads and shows them as \fBepx vendors list\fR does.
.PP
Changes nothing: Emporix serves this read as POST with a JSON body, which the flags make or \fB\-\-body\fR gives whole.
.PP
Requires the vendor.vendor_read scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-body <FILE>\fR
Send the JSON request body in FILE as given (\- reads standard input) instead of the one the other flags make.
.TP
\fB\-\-columns <names>\fR
Print only these columns of table and csv, in this order: comma\-separated names (any case) among ID, NAME, TYPE, PARENT, LEGAL NAME, COUNTRY.
.TP
\fB\-\-limit <n>\fR
Print at most n items; paged reads stop early where they safely can (0: every item).
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-headers\fR
Print table and csv without the header row.
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Output format: table, json, yaml or csv (csv: the table\(aqs rows; json and yaml: the whole response). Default: \fBtable\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-query <filter>\fR
Emporix q filter, sent as given in the request body, not in the URL (empty: no filter), e.g. code:(A1,A2); space\-separated conditions must all match (fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-sort <order>\fR
Emporix sort order, passed as given, e.g. code or name.en:desc,code; fields mostly as in \fB\-o json\fR (Emporix may ignore an unknown one).
.TP
\fB\-\-stream\fR
Print items as JSON Lines as soon as they are checked, page by page on paged lists, reading up to 10000 pages where a list without it stops after 1000: a check failing on a later page exits 1 after the pages before it (excludes \fB\-o\fR, \fB\-\-columns\fR and \fB\-\-no\-headers\fR).
.SS "epx vendors update"
Upsert one vendor.
.PP
.RS "4"
.nf
epx vendors update ID [flags]
.fi
.RE
.PP
Replaces the vendor ID with the JSON body of \fB\-\-file\fR, shaped as create takes it but without an id, or creates it with that id where none exists (an upsert); it requires name and type. With metadata.version as \fBepx vendors get ID \-o json\fR prints it, Emporix replaces it only if nobody changed it since, and answers 409 Conflict (exit 5) otherwise; without metadata.version, it replaces it whatever its version. ID is the ID that \fBepx vendors list\fR shows.
.PP
Changes data: on a terminal, epx asks before it sends PUT. \fB\-\-yes\fR sends without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-); \fB\-\-dry\-run\fR prints the request instead of sending it.
.PP
Requires the vendor.vendor_manage scope.
.PP
\fBOptions:\fR
.TP
\fB\-\-dry\-run\fR
Print the request instead of sending it (excludes \fB\-o\fR).
.TP
\fB\-\-file <PATH>\fR
JSON request body in PATH, sent byte for byte (\- reads standard input; sending it then needs \fB\-\-yes\fR; required).
.TP
\fB\-o, \-\-output <format>\fR
Format of the response: json or yaml. Default: \fBjson\fR.
.TP
\fB\-\-yes\fR
Send without asking (required without a terminal, or with \fB\-\-file\fR \-).
.SH "SEE ALSO"
\fBepx\fR(1) for the global options, the credentials epx reads and its exit codes; https://commerce-cloud-integrations.github.io/emporix-cli/commands/vendors
